+# Metered usage billing (#69)
+
+Customers on the new API plans pay for what they use. This adds the billing
+side of metered plans; collecting usage events stays in the usage pipeline.
+
+## What changes
+
+`src/billing.ts`
+- `usageInPeriod(records, period)` sums the quantity of the usage records
+  whose UTC day falls in the billing period. Periods keep their usual meaning:
+  `start` inclusive, `end` exclusive (the next period starts on `end`).
+- `tieredCharge(units, tiers)` prices units with graduated tiers: with tiers
+  `[{ upTo: 1000, 0.10 }, { upTo: null, 0.05 }]`, units 1-1000 cost 0.10 each
+  and every unit above 1000 costs 0.05. Tiers may be passed in any order.
+- `usageCharge(plan, records, period, activatedAt)` bills usage above the
+  plan's included units. A subscription activated mid-period gets included
+  units in proportion to the whole days it was active, rounded up in the
+  customer's favour.
+
+`src/invoice.ts`
+- `Invoice.addUsageLine(description, charge, taxRate)` adds the usage charge
+  as one line and skips periods with no billable usage, so invoices never show
+  zero-amount usage lines.
+
+## Testing
+
+New `tests/billing-usage.test.ts`.
